    "notes": [
        "<b>Writing Intensive Courses:</b> Students must take 3 courses: 1 First Year (UWRT-150 or ISTE-110), 1 Gen Ed, & 1 program specific (CSCI-472)",
        "<b>Lab Sciences:</b> Only specific sequences are allowed in Biology, Chemistry or Physics. Please see the CS BS/MS course page.",
        "<b>DSCI Electives:</b> Only specific courses are allowed. Please see the CS handbook or talk to an academic advisor.",
        "<b>CS/DSCI Electives:</b> Only specific courses are allowed. Please see the Data Science MS Advisor for a list of CSCI graduate courses that can be chosen to meet this requirement.",
        "<b>SWEN Waive:</b> CS students have the SWEN 601 requirement for the MS in Data Science waived based on their prior coursework, and in its place a 4th graduate elective course is taken.",
        "<b>Condition:</b> If approved DSCI Graduate Electives that are Computer Science (CSCI) courses are selected as all of the double-counts, the BS double-count can satisfy CS Elective requirements instead of Open Electives.  In this case, the double-counting courses would be the ** CS Elective courses in Year 4 along with the * CS Elective course in Year 5.  DSCI 633 and STAT 614 would still be taken as listed in Year 4, but would contribute only to the MS DSCI credit total.  Correspondingly, two DSCI Graduate Elective courses listed in Year 6 convert to Open Elective courses contributing only to the BS in CS." 
    ]
